    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with high-ceiling opportunities concentrated at the top of the order. **Jackson Merrill** (74.47) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.04) are our primary engines, benefiting significantly from favorable matchups against Elder and Martinez. **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) also presents an elite play, as he draws the day\u2019s most exploitable matchup against Bratt (7.04 xERA). While **Drake Baldwin** (68.13) sits near the top, his elevated score is buoyed by his leadoff position and strong xwOBA, proving that volume at the top of the lineup remains a critical stabilizer for our daily production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Curtis Mead** on the bench despite his 52.30 efficiency score. While **Curtis Mead** benefits from a high-park-factor environment against Freeland, his negative platoon split against the left-handed starter left him just shy of the threshold set by **Coby Mayo** (54.83) and **Liam Hicks** (52.55), who occupy higher leverage spots. Risk mitigation remains a theme today; **Luis Robert Jr.** (40.13) and **Andy Pages** (48.03) are severely hampered by facing Misiorowski (2.20 xERA) and S\u00e1nchez (2.85 xERA), respectively. We are effectively starting these high-upside assets at the bottom of our roster depth, but with the scarcity of speed, we are monitoring their efficiency closely to avoid burning game caps against elite arms. \n\nThe primary threat to our consistency today is **Sam Antonacci** (47.20), who faces the tall task of hitting against deGrom. While his leadoff spot provides a small buffer, the diminished SP skill profile makes this a marginal play. We are maintaining a disciplined approach, as the heavy emphasis on **Nasim Nunez** (56.05) and his speed profile continues to be our hedge against a tight league race in the SB category. If any of our middle-of-the-pack options like **Heliot Ramos** (56.48) underperform early, we are prepared to shift focus toward maximizing our late-game potential from the bench.",
